From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Simon Elsbrock <simon@iodev.org>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 16:37:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mtd: nandx: add MediaTek's MT8519 SPI-NAND driver, ported to
 6.12

The Echo Dot (5th gen) boots from SPI-NAND (ADR 0035), and Pinna finds its
root in a UBI volume there. MediaTek's self-contained nandx driver from
Amazon's 5.4 release (the kernel subset: the core, the SPI-NAND and NFI
layers, the bad-block table and the platform glue), built with a kbuild
Makefile. Two changes for 6.12: drop mtd_info._block_unmarkbad (removed
upstream), and nand_remove() returns void (the platform_driver .remove
signature changed). It matches the DT's mediatek,mt8519-nfc.

Builds into the kernel and links; off in every current variant.
